Serve the web client behind a trusted proxy with no pairing prompt

Stock `orca serve` delivers its pairing token only in the URL fragment, but a
Coder tile URL is fixed at template-build time, so a stock tile lands on a
"paste a pairing code" form. Trusted mode solves it the way code-server's
`--auth none` does: bind the runtime WS listener to loopback and trust the proxy
that already authenticated, exposing the offer over a loopback-gated
`GET /trusted-session`. Orca's E2EE is intact - only the credential's delivery
moved from the fragment to a loopback fetch.

The web client dials same-origin from `window.location`, so the tile needs no
`--pairing-address`, and on `auth-failed` it re-probes and adopts a new offer.
Trusted-session devices are named "Web session <date>" so the shared-access list
reads honestly.

To test, open the workspace tile: the full Orca web UI should load with no
pairing prompt. See `static-web-client-handler.test.ts` - the endpoint serves
the offer with `Cache-Control: no-store` to a loopback peer, 404s a non-loopback
one, 503s before an offer can be minted, works behind a path prefix, and is
absent entirely when trusted-proxy mode is off.

